0021 — TEX_QUAD takes its sampling taps once per column and once per row.

A pixel's u in TEX_QUAD depends on its column alone and its v on its row
alone, yet the loop evaluated both for every pixel: two f32 expressions
and two saturating casts, and for a linear texture four texel reads and
four blends even where both weights were 0. The taps are now taken once
per column into a table and once per row, from the same f32 expressions,
and the pixel loop only fetches and blends:

- a tap on a texel centre is that texel, because `lerp8(a, b, 0)` is `a`:
  every nearest tap, and nearly every linear tap of a quad drawn at its
  texture's own size, reads one texel instead of four;
- an RGBA8888 texel of alpha 0 at such a tap is skipped before it is read,
  because it is still 0 after the modulate and every target's `blend`
  returns without writing at 0;
- every other tap is the four-texel blend it was.

The pixels are byte-identical by construction, not by tolerance: the
taps come out of the expressions the per-pixel loop evaluated, and a
centre is decided by the weights the blend would have used. That matters
at a texture's own size, where `(j + 0.5) / w * w` lands a fraction below
the centre on some columns (229 of 1080 at w = 1080; at w = 41 the first
column, whose tap then leans on the second texel). Those columns keep the
four-texel blend; a shortcut that assumed centres differs there by up to
2 levels, and on such a first column by the whole step to the next texel.

By file:
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: `linear_axis` and `nearest_axis` (one axis
  of a lookup; `linear_sample_coordinates` is two `linear_axis` calls and
  returns what it did), `bilinear` (the four-texel blend `sample_linear`
  held), and `tex_quad`'s loop. A test keeps the per-pixel sampler as a
  reference and compares it with `tex_quad` byte for byte, on the RGBA and
  RGB565 targets, over 24 textures (1x1 to 100x3, RGBA8888 with every
  fifth texel transparent and RGB565, nearest and linear) and seven quads
  each (own size, own size clipped, 2x, fractional, minified, a UV
  sub-rect, mirrored), two modulates, scale 1 and 2, whole frame and a
  damage region. With the "own size means centre" shortcut in its place
  it fails on the 25x27 linear texture.

